---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Managed cloud" description="Inspect the live LiteMCP Composer managed-cloud preview, its current Cloudflare-backed deployment evidence, and the acceptance work that remains before general availability.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Managed cloud · Preview"
    title="The managed-cloud preview is live."
    description="The public site and Worker run at litemcpcomposer.com. Health, readiness, authentication routing, storage bindings, TLS, and canonical-domain behavior have deployment evidence; privileged onboarding and MCP workflows remain preview acceptance work."
    signal="Public preview · signups closed by default"
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a class="button button--primary button--large" href="/app">Open the preview console</a>
      <a class="button button--large" href="/pricing">Compare distributions</a>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Managed cloud contract"
        title="Convenience without a closed product fork."
        description="The preview runs the complete public product core. A separate private control plane handles customer lifecycle, hosted entitlements, billing, support access, provisioning, and fleet releases."
      />
      <div class="two-column-cards">
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Preview</p>
          <h2>The current management slice</h2>
          <p>Server registration, composition creation, scoped sessions, policy simulation, approval records, audit, and export are present at preview maturity.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Preview</p>
          <h2>Portable package boundary</h2>
          <p>Configuration export and shared packages exist. A live import and execution test from managed cloud to Kubernetes has not yet passed.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Published preview defaults</p>
          <h2>Fair-use limits are explicit</h2>
          <p>Each hosted-preview organization receives 5 servers, 5 compositions, 25 active sessions, and 1,000 tool calls per UTC day. Self-hosted deployments do not inherit these commercial limits.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Product commitment</p>
          <h2>Metadata-first operations</h2>
          <p>Service telemetry should not require tool arguments, tool responses, access tokens, or provider secrets.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--subtle">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div class="split-layout__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current status</p>
        <h2>Deployment proof exists; product acceptance is incomplete.</h2>
        <p>
          The Worker, static assets, TLS routes, dedicated KV/D1 resources, remote auth migration,
          health/readiness, unauthenticated session endpoint, and apex/www routing passed on 21 July
          2026. First-admin onboarding, privileged control-plane use, MCP initialize/list/call,
          rollback, load, and external security acceptance have not passed.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-note">
        Catalog projections still use eventually consistent KV storage, while the current
        composition routes security-sensitive authority through a Durable Object boundary.
        Multi-writer parity, recovery, availability, regional placement, durability, and support
        targets remain unproven. <a href="https://github.com/reachjalil/liteMCP/blob/main/docs/managed-cloud-fair-use.md">Read the fair-use boundary ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
